  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "In a certain population the ratio of the number of women to the number of men is \\(11\\) to \\(10.\\) If the average (arithmetic mean) age of the women is \\(34\\) and the average age of the men is \\(32,\\) then the average age of the population is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(32\\frac9{10}\\)",
    "B": "\\(32\\frac{20}{21}\\)",
    "C": "\\(33\\)",
    "D": "\\(33\\frac1{21}\\)",
    "E": "\\(33\\frac1{10}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The two group averages must be weighted by their group sizes, since every person contributes once to the population average. Write the numbers of women and men as \\(11k\\) and \\(10k\\), respectively, where \\(k>0\\). Their total ages are \\(34(11k)\\) and \\(32(10k)\\). Thus the population average is\n\\[\n\\frac{34(11k)+32(10k)}{11k+10k}\n=\\frac{374+320}{21}\n=\\frac{694}{21}\n=\\boxed{33\\frac1{21}}.\n\\]\nThe average age is \\(33\\frac1{21}\\) years, choice D.",
